WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.040
After receiving a threatening letter from Hells Maestro,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.710
we went to the mountain mansion
of the violinist, Yuge Masaomi.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:50.300
Here he was going to give his famous violin,
the "Testa di Drago", to one of his successors.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:56.560
But at the same time, one of his students,
Shirase Amina, was killed by someone.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.110
And what’s worse is that we were sealed in by an
unnatural landslide which occurred during a typhoon.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.400
And then there was a second murder.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:09.610
Ryuu!

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.280
You! How dare you!

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.240
What's going on?

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.250
Melody of Death

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.050
Murasame-kun!

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.300
Amakusa-kun, what is this?

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:31.590
I don’t know.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.890
I was talking with him while he was eating
when he suddenly started screaming in pain.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.530
It's no good, he's dead.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:42.700
No.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:43.740
Why?

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.160
Did you do it?

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.290
No!

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.200
He died right in front of me.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.700
There's probably poison in his drink.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:53.700
Poison?

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.080
What was he drinking?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.410
Whiskey from the counter.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.510
Cyanide.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.350
I smell almonds.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.060
This Is it.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:22.270
Then the poison that killed him was in this whiskey?

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.490
What?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.440
Arisa, what is the meaning of this?

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.900
No!

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.530
I don’t know!

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.910
But you’re the most suspicious person!

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.910
No, anybody could have had the chance
to put poison into his bottle.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.580
Stop trying to decide who did
it using such simplistic ideas!

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.510
You're just saying that because
you did it, aren’t you?

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.300
Hey, say something!

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:58.060
Now that you mention it, you and him
didn’t seem to be getting along.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.980
You killed Murasame!

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.020
Stop it!

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.240
Kyuu!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:12.860
We’re here to solve this case by the order of the
head of DDS, the famous detective Dan Morihiko.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:18.660
None of us would ever do something
to hurt the name of DDS!

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.910
Then who did it?

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.290
Stop it!

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.000
Yuge-sensei!

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.590
Stop blaming each other in front of his corpse.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.230
Sensei!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.800
Let us leave this to them and return to our rooms.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.440
I need to tell Kinta and Hongou-sensei.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:50.450
Kyuu.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:52.990
Thanks.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:55.700
Nothing.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.280
My clothes are stained with blood. I'll go change.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.920
This brilliant scheme.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.050
If they’re involved in this murder...

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:22.260
Ryuu, people cannot run away from their destiny.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:27.560
Whether you like it or not, you will...

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:28.650
Dammit!

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.370
I see. It’s possible!

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:56.300
Dammit! When are we gonna get there?

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.590
I'm hungry!

00:05:58.990 --> 00:05:59.970
Did you say something?

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.890
No. I don’t need to eat, I’m just fine!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.060
Then you don’t need this meal bar.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.360
Here you go, Gotouda-san.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.860
This old man... He's got food?

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.740
Thank you.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.620
Hongou-san, you're certainly well prepared.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.490
I am a detective.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:30.330
It’s always possible that sudden trouble will prevent
me from getting food so I carry it with me.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.840
I guess I’m just not prepared then.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:35.840
Touyama.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.130
Do you know the meaning of what I just said?

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.260
A detective always needs to be prepared, right?

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.890
And if there’s someone who’s not
a detective, but well prepared?

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.730
What does that mean?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:53.440
Don’t you know?

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:54.980
They’re the criminal.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.280
Shirase

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:03.320
Look at this.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:07.580
These shards of pottery are covered
blood as if a geyser exploded.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:13.790
This means that they were on the
floor while she was still alive.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.920
In other words, she was killed while she
was still alive but was unable to move.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.550
What does that mean?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.550
Kyuu, get everybody together in Murasame-san’s
room on the 2nd floor.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.100
I want to run an experiment.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.270
An experiment?

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.100
Murasame

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.900
What is this?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.270
To think you'd call us into Murasame-kun’s
room when he'd just died.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.610
What are you going to do?

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.400
Kyuu, do it.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.300
This is...

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:52.160
Think of this as Shirase-san.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.920
The position of this room is exactly
the same as Shirase’s room below,

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.800
and everything is mostly in the same place.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.060
So?

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.340
The criminal put Shirase to sleep
with some kind of tranquilizer

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:09.810
and set the knife up just above
her carotid artery just like this.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.440
Why would they do that?

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:16.650
As a trick to give the real criminal an alibi.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:17.730
Alibi?

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:18.650
Trick?

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:25.740
When we heard that sound of something shattering,
the criminal was already gone from the room.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:32.620
Most likely, the criminal set her up here like this

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:40.090
and then used the candlesticks as a brace for the
knife, which they placed just above her neck.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:45.840
And when the right time came,
the flowerpot fell from above.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:58.020
How did they drop the flowerpot?

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.860
And at just the right time?

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.900
Meg, show her.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.040
What are you doing?

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:19.420
This is...

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.090
There are a lot of low ranges on this song.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:28.550
This was on before “The
Banquet” when Shirase was killed.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.060
The pot is moving!

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:40.700
Why?

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:54.040
The knife is stuck in the neck just
like it was when Shirase died!

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:56.960
Why?

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:59.460
Why did the pot move on its own?

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:01.880
Resonant frequency!

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:08.010
It is the phenomenon where matter vibrates in response
to certain frequencies, corresponding to its size.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.720
In other words, the size of that pot meant
that it resonated with the song

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:17.690
that was being played very loud at
that time, and it began to vibrate.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:22.020
That was the crash sound that we heard then?

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:23.570
Wait a second.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:30.910
How then, do you explain that her room was
filled with bits of shattered glass and china?

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.370
There wasn’t just one crash.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:38.120
The whole mansion was filled with
the sound of glass breaking!

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:40.370
Meg, keep going.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:42.350
Yes.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.180
What is this?

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.590
Why is there that kind of sound on the CD?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:58.520
This isn’t a CD, it’s an MD.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:01.600
An MD? Then...

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:17.120
Thus, by filling the room with bits of broken
glass and pottery, and putting on the music

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:22.000
with the sounds of shattering mixed in, they made
it look like there was a fight in her room.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:29.170
But who did that then?

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:36.600
That I can’t say for certain, but when you think of
when they must have broken the pottery and glass,

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.060
I think you can get an idea.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.190
Only one person could done it.

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:50.820
The only one who it could have been was... YOU!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.730
The only one who it could have been was... YOU!

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.480
Kirishima Sorata-san!

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.280
What are you saying?

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.530
Why me?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:21.200
Of the eight people in this mansion, the only one
who could have broken those things was you.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:27.540
If the sounds were recorded on the MD
then doesn’t everybody lose their alibi?

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:33.300
Even we, who were in the attic, heard
the sounds of the shattering.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:40.430
That means that there’s no way that everybody
wouldn’t hear them actually breaking.

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.310
Except for that one time.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.810
That’s right! When everyone was in the music hall!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.110
That hall has such thick soundproof walls, we
couldn’t hear anything happening outside!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:56.490
And the only person who left the
room at that time was you.

00:12:57.470 --> 00:13:02.660
Now that you mention it, the minute sensei started
his performance you turned pale and left.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.120
I didn’t kill her!

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:14.000
If you didn’t do it then why did you
leave during my performance?

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:15.630
Well...

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.800
I can hear...

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.180
Houshou Mitsuru.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:30.480
I can hear her playing “The Demon’s Banquet”!

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.900
What?

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.900
Kirishima-san, stop your bad acting and admit it!

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.490
It’s not me!

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:41.450
Kirishima-kun!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.780
It’s not me!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.580
Kirishima-san!

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.750
What happened; Ryuu?

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:53.040
That wasn’t like you at all!

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:09.230
Um, Kirishima-san, can I come in for a second?

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.230
I'm coming in.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.440
Treating people like criminals!

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.440
You DDS people are idiots!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.070
I’m sorry about earlier.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.660
I’m very sorry!

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:31.580
Kirishima-san, why are you afraid of Houshou
Mitsuru... and “The Demon’s Banquet"?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.800
I get phone calls.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:37.630
Phone calls?

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.970
I get them
a violin playing from the other end.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:45.180
Houshou Mitsuru’s “The Demon’s Banquet”.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.390
Not just me. Everyone gets them.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:54.400
Houshou Mitsuru is back from
and is taking revenge on us!

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:55.730
Revenge?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.320
It’s nothing.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:14:59.320
Get out!

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.410
I'll help you.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.160
Thank you.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:11.960
Huh?

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.120
This is...

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.960
What's wrong?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.750
There’s a deep mark in the floor.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:32.270
Meg!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:33.520
Kyuu !

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:36.060
I've seen something weird!

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:37.480
Weird?

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:42.440
It might be an important hint in Shirase-san’s murder!

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.490
Didn’t I completely solve that trick a while ago?

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.040
I’m going to test that now!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:56.880
It might not work too well, but if a detective
gives up the case it will never be solved!

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.340
All right, I'll do it.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.970
He’s moving at his own pace as always.

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.220
I just can’t beat him.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:14.600
Even with a bit of intelligence or deductive skills,
that alone isn’t enough to be a detective.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.940
When I look at Kyuu, I think of that somehow.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.440
That’s Kazuma.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:23.360
Yeah?

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:24.740
Meg?

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:29.200
I’ve found out the truth of Houshou Mitsuru’s suicide.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:35.160
Two months before she died, she lost all
the fingers on both hands in an accident.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.250
Lost?

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:47.930
Yes. In mid-January this year, she headed out from the
mansion you're in to go to a last-minute concert.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:53.720
But she ran out of gas halfway there in a blizzard.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:58.810
That area has temperatures around
15 below freezing in winter,

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:01.860
and unfortunately her car had broken
down so she couldn’t call for help.

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:07.030
Left with no other choice, she
walked for miles in the snow.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:10.950
When the other students came for her it was too late.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:15.830
And she lost most of her fingers on her hands to frostbite.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:17.710
How awful.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.080
To a violinist, her fingers are her life.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:22.960
If that happened...

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.630
But that “accident” is a bit suspicious.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:31.220
The problem was due to four separate
incidents of bad luck;

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:38.520
and it looks like the four students who were fighting
over the Testa di Drago were behind it.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.150
Her first bit of bad luck was the concert

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:45.690
which Gotouda Manabu suddenly decided
to hold in the middle of a blizzard.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:52.240
Her second bit of bad luck was that she’d lent her cell to
Murasame Shion, who just happened to drop it in a lake.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:59.000
Her third bit of bad luck was that Sonata took the car
out the day before and used up almost all the gas.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:06.050
And fourth, Shirase Mayumi went skiing, borrowing
her gloves and heavy winter clothes.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:09.680
That’s too much to be a coincidence.

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.300
You're right.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:13.390
By the way, where’s Kinta?

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.430
Isn’t he there yet?

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.850
It’s already 11.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:21.770
Look, Touyama.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.230
There’s another landslide.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:29.950
Wait!

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:33.570
I can see the mansion’s lights above!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.200
If we go up this cliff, can’t we get there?

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.540
Looks like that’s our only option.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:47.300
It’s not here. Like I thought. Nowhere to be found.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:51.880
That means that the trick the criminal used was
more complex than Ryuu had originally thought!

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.430
Hey, are you able to keep up with me?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.690
Yeah, I’m fine.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:03.730
Not you. Gotouda-san!

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:06.110
Huh?

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:07.980
I can’t see him.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:09.570
Hey!

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:12.360
Gotouda-san, where are you?

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.240
I'm here!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:16.330
There he is.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:20.790
I'm fine, go on ahead.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:22.870
I'll take a rest and...

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.380
Gotouda-san!

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.670
Gotouda-san!

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.300
Where are you?

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:34.720
What?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:39.720
The four of them worked together
to cause Houshou’s accident?

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:42.930
It is quite a large possibility.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:51.440
Her talent was incredible.

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:56.450
To the point that even the other students
had no choice but to accept it.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:07.500
Yuge-sensei, have you decided which of your
Students will get the Testa di Drago?

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:12.710
All five of them are extremely talented.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:17.180
But amongst them are two whose talents
are found only once in a generation.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:18.350
Two?

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:22.640
But there is but one Testa di Drago.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:27.940
Excuse us.

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:33.530
Hey!

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:34.610
Kyuu!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:38.570
We found out the truth behind Houshou Mitsuru's death.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:39.910
Really?

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:40.950
I found something too.

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:44.330
Yes?

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:49.170
Gotouda-san fell off a cliff?

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:50.590
What?

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.590
11:40 already!

00:20:57.990 --> 00:21:00.800
Already 10 minutes since he fell!

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:17.070
“The Demon’s Banquet” won't leave my mind!

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:27.370
Yes.

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:34.550
Dammit. I can’t find him.

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:36.260
Where did they go?

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:37.630
No Kinta!

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.340
If a detective gives up...

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.890
What are we going to do if YOU fall!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:47.560
I’m scared.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:51.690
That’s...

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:54.980
Gotouda-san!

00:21:58.590 --> 00:21:59.950
We’re lucky, he’s alive.

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:03.330
Gotouda-san, wake up!

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.910
Hongou-san... I ...

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:10.120
You fell from the cliff.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:12.000
What happened?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.340
I felt like somebody pushed me from behind.

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:20.510
My violin!

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:23.640
It’s right here.

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:29.600
To be pushed in a place like this...

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:32.900
Is that the doing of Hell’s Maestro?

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:37.820
Gotouda-san!

00:22:38.470 --> 00:22:40.030
What happened?

00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:42.360
He fell from that cliff.

00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:46.160
Arisa-kun, Shiba-san, where is everybody?

00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:50.870
The only students of Yuge-sensei who are
still alive are you and Kirishima-kun.

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:54.840
Kirishima is safe?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:56.090
He’s in his room.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:57.250
I'll go get him.

00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:58.880
Let me go too.

00:22:59.650 --> 00:23:00.340
Me too!

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:02.880
Gotouda-kun.

00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:05.890
Sensei, I'm sorry.

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:08.520
Something terrible has happened.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.600
Kirishima-kun, it’s me.

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:16.110
Gotouda-san is here.

00:23:17.050 --> 00:23:19.690
That’s odd. Is he asleep?

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:22.150
Let’s open it.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.290
Kirishima-san.

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:43.010
A syringe?

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.530 --> 00:24:50.670
The truth behind the skillfully planned serial murders.

00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:53.840
At last the identity of Hell’s Maestro is revealed!

00:24:54.370 --> 00:24:57.140
And during that time, the terrifying
trap of Pluto was activated!

00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:58.600
The target is the Q Class.

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:03.560
Can they solve all the mysteries and play the
final notes of this capriccio of murder?

00:25:04.210 --> 00:25:05.230
There is one answer!

00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:08.770
Useful knowledge corner!

00:25:09.380 --> 00:25:13.740
You'll often hear of people who've drunk
cyanide as “smelling of almonds”,

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:20.380
but that’s the sour smell of the seed of the
almond tree, not the smell of the nuts.
